#!/usr/bin/env node
// =============================================================================
// baritone-runner.mjs — HTTP wrapper around a HeadlessMc + Baritone MC client.
//
// One node process per bot. Command wire = HMC launcher stdin.
// State wire  = the game client's own <gameDir>/logs/latest.log tail.
// NO RCON anywhere in this file. LAW.
//
// Launch recipe below is the FIELD-PROVEN one from cave/BARITONE.md
// ("Round 2 FINAL update — verdict: WORKS", 2026-09-01) as first proven by
// hmc-launch8.mjs. Do not "improve" the three load-bearing quirks:
//   1. NO  -lwjgl               -> the headless render stub hangs forever on
//                                  1.21.11 blur-pipeline uniforms. Real GPU +
//                                  hidden real window instead.
//   2. NO  --quickPlayMultiplayer -> silently never fires on this HMC/MC pair.
//                                  Join is driven manually by writing
//                                  `connect <host> <port>` to launcher stdin
//                                  once the title screen is up (~35 s).
//   3. YES -Dhmc.jline.enabled=false -> hmc-specifics spins a SECOND JLine
//                                  reader inside Minecraft.<init>; over a
//                                  plain (non-TTY) pipe it throws
//                                  IllegalStateException and kills the client.
//                                  The softer hmc.jline.dumb.* flags do NOT
//                                  fix this one.
// =============================================================================
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PINNED VERSIONS  — every artifact below is an explicit, on-disk, pinned file.
//                    NOTHING in this runner resolves a "latest" URL or tag.
//                    The runner never downloads: preflight() fails loudly if a
//                    pinned file is missing rather than fetching a replacement.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   Java runtime      : 21.0.10   C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-21.0.10\bin\java.exe
//   HeadlessMc launcher: 2.10.0   bots/<NAME>/headlessmc-launcher.jar
//                                 (sha-identical copy of
//                                  shared/headlessmc-launcher.jar)
//   Minecraft         : 1.21.11
//   Fabric loader     : 0.19.3    version id `fabric-loader-0.19.3-1.21.11`
//                                 installed under the SHARED mc install
//                                 (%APPDATA%\.minecraft\versions\...)
//   Fabric API mod    : 0.141.6+1.21.11
//                                 fabric-api-0.141.6+1.21.11.jar
//   Baritone          : 1.17.0    baritone-standalone-fabric-1.17.0.jar
//                                 (cabaletta official, built FOR 1.21.11)
//   hmc-specifics     : 2.4.0     hmc-specifics-1.21.11-2.4.0-fabric-release.jar
//                                 (the version-stamped file HMC itself cached
//                                  under HeadlessMC/specifics/ — NOT the
//                                  "-latest" named download in shared/, which
//                                  would double-load as a second copy of the
//                                  same mod and crash fabric)
//
//   HMC_LAUNCH_TARGET below is the launcher's version selector. It is matched
//   against the installed version id `fabric-loader-0.19.3-1.21.11`, which is
//   the only fabric version installed — so it is unambiguous, not a "latest".
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PER-INSTANCE gameDir — how two bots are kept from colliding
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HeadlessMc 2.10.0 ignores the launcher process cwd when choosing the game

